# Build output and installed packages.
node_modules/
dist/

# Real environment values. .env.example is tracked and documents every key.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# The service's leaderboard and challenge snapshot. Everything in it is public
# by design, but it is runtime state rather than source, so it stays out.
.data/
*.tmp

# Planning and internal docs. The public repo gets the README, which is written
# for someone arriving cold. PLAN.md is the build spec with its locked-decisions
# table, docs/ holds the submission checklist, the deploy runbook and the
# marketing plan. All useful, none of it anyone else's business.
PLAN.md

# Note the star. Git cannot re-include anything whose parent directory is
# excluded, so ignoring `docs/` outright would make the exception below silently
# do nothing. Excluding the CONTENTS leaves the directory itself visible, which
# is what lets one subfolder back in.
docs/*

# The README's screenshots, which are public by definition. Generated by
# scripts/shoot.mjs, and the README is unreadable without them.
!docs/shots/

# The stage guide, which the README links to. It is the overflow for the part of
# the README that would otherwise be seven long sections, so it is as public as
# the README is. Without this line the link is a 404 for everybody but us, and
# nothing about the local checkout would show it.
!docs/stage-1-to-7.md

# The 250 word description the submission portal asks for. Kept in the repo so
# the text that was submitted is the text in version control, rather than a
# paragraph that only ever existed in a form field.
!docs/description.md

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.log
# Stray dev-server output. Runtime noise, never source.
*.err

# package-lock.json is deliberately NOT ignored. Pinned installs are the whole
# point of committing it, and a mini app that builds differently on the judge's
# machine than on yours is a mini app you cannot debug.

PLAN-V2.md

# v3 planning. Private, like the other plans.
PLAN-V3.md

# Deploy keys, and anything else shaped like a private key.
#
# A key was generated into this directory during CI setup and sat here untracked
# while `git add -A` ran several times. It was never committed, but only because
# of timing. A private key in a public repository is the worst single mistake
# available here, so the pattern is broad on purpose: it catches openssh keys,
# PEM files and the usual id_* names regardless of what anyone remembers to do.
sface-deploy
sface-deploy.pub
*.pem
*.key
id_ed25519*
id_rsa*

# Throwaway browser profile from scripts/shoot.mjs. Regenerated on every run and
# full of cache nobody wants in a diff.
.shoot-profile/

# The launch video's working directory: captured frames, encoded shots, the
# narration clips and the export. Hundreds of megabytes of PNGs and MP4s that
# are all rebuildable from scripts/record.mjs, build-video.mjs and
# finish-video.mjs, so the recipe is tracked and the output is not.
.video/
